Run one of the commands berth.toml declares under [commands], in this registered
worktree, with the worktree's BERTH_* environment and BERTH_COMMAND naming it.
Everything after -- is passed to the command. It runs on the terminal, so it can
prompt and answer Ctrl-C itself, and its output is this command's own; its exit
code becomes berth run's. Unless it sets lock = false, it holds the worktree's
lock while it runs. docs/hooks.md has the details.

Usage:
  berth run [name] [-- args...] [flags]

Flags:
  -h, --help   help for run

Global Flags:
      --config string   path to berth.toml (default: nearest above cwd)
  -V, --version         output the version number
